.TH XUR.STD.SYNC 7 "2026-10-27" "xur 0.1.1" "Xur Manual"
.SH NAME
xur.std.sync \- channels for sending values between threads
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B use std::sync;
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B std::sync
provides channels for inter-thread communication.
.B channel()
returns a
.RI ( Sender ", " Receiver )
pair.
.SH FUNCTIONS
.TP
.B channel() -> (Sender, Receiver)
Create a new channel. Multiple senders can be cloned from the same sender;
there is one receiver.
.SS Sender methods
.TP
.B send(value) -> Result<(), str>
Send a value to the receiver. Returns an error if the receiver has been
dropped.
.SS Receiver methods
.TP
.B recv() -> Option<Value>
Block until a value arrives, or return
.B None
if all senders are gone.
.TP
.B try_recv() -> Option<Value>
Return a value if one is already waiting, otherwise
.BR None .
.SH EXAMPLES
.nf
use std::sync;
use std::thread;
use std::io;

fn main() {
    let (tx, rx) = sync::channel();
    thread::spawn(|| {
        tx.send("hello from another thread").unwrap();
    });
    io::println("{}", rx.recv().unwrap());
}
.fi
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR xur.std (7),
.BR xur.std.thread (7)
